steps.body:
How many rooms do a day's meetings need at once? Sort the start times and the end times separately, then sweep through the starts in order with a pointer `e` into the ends. A meeting that starts before the earliest end still pending finds every room taken, so you need one more. Otherwise some meeting has ended, and its room is reused: move `e` on.

```java harness
int[] starts = {0, 5, 10, 15};
int[] ends = {10, 15, 20, 30};
{{code}}
System.out.println(rooms);
```

```java
int rooms = 0;
int e = 0;
for (int s : starts) {
    if (s < ends[e]) {
        rooms++;          // nothing has ended yet: open a room
    } else {
        e++;              // a meeting ended: take its room
    }
}
```

`rooms` never goes down, because a reused room was counted when it opened. A meeting that ends at 10 frees its room for one that starts at 10, since `10 < 10` is false.

Copy the two columns out of the `int[][]` first, with `starts[i] = meetings[i][0]` and `ends[i] = meetings[i][1]`, then `Arrays.sort` each one. Sorting them apart breaks up the pairs, and that is fine: the count only depends on how many meetings have started and how many have ended at each moment.

example.code:
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = sc.nextInt();
        int[][] meetings = new int[n][2];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            meetings[i][0] = sc.nextInt();
            meetings[i][1] = sc.nextInt();
        }

        int[] starts = new int[n];
        int[] ends = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            starts[i] = meetings[i][0];
            ends[i] = meetings[i][1];
        }
        Arrays.sort(starts);
        Arrays.sort(ends);
        System.out.println("Starts: " + Arrays.toString(starts));
        System.out.println("Ends: " + Arrays.toString(ends));

        int rooms = 0;
        int e = 0;
        for (int s : starts) {
            if (s < ends[e]) {
                rooms++;
            } else {
                e++;
            }
        }
        System.out.println("Rooms: " + rooms);
    }
}

